{
  "description": "A chat's approval state as the host holds it (agent#53), and what it admits: no grant; a ready grant for a pack update; the same grant used, stale and revoked; and a ready grant for a Dialect publication of one named target. checks holds, for one item (state, its index) at one time (now), a commit request and the resource as the host resolves it then: the mode the host shows (auto only where a grant is ready and not past expiresAt), whether the commit is admitted, the grant's state after (used where admitted, consumed before the commit runs and never replayed; expired at or past expiresAt; stale where the request's or the resource's revision is not the grant's) and the refusal's words where it is not. A commit is admitted only for one of the four actions, by the grant's own id, for its action, path, name and target, on its revision, before it expires. No run mints a grant: the person's decision does, and no approval crosses the engine slot. Written by hand from the Desk server's transaction; the harness carries no approval reader (the host's), so go/gate is held to it, and the schema.",
